  "name": "Casting Desecrate always triggers Shadowstorm, even when the cone misses everything (#9492)",
  "contract": "Shadowstorm 520277's Description reads 'Casting Desecrate always triggers Shadowstorm', an unconditional cast-gated clause contrasted against the damage-chance-gated Pommel Smash clause in the same tooltip. Before the fix, the trigger ran through the native spell_proc dispatcher (HitMask 9283: normal/crit/block/absorb/full-block only, excluding miss/dodge/parry) and a C++ Direct(event) check requiring nonzero damage, so a Desecrate cone that connected with nothing never produced a Shadowstorm. QA Test 100% Reduced Hit Chance 10048 (SPELL_AURA_MOD_HIT_CHANCE, -199) on the caster forces every Desecrate swing to miss (zero damage, no proc event), isolating the miss path #5807's guaranteed-hit fixture cannot exercise; the fixture harness can only set_aura on a player actor, so the miss is forced on the caster's own hit chance rather than the target's dodge. The trigger is gated on the Shadowstorm talent/passive 520277 itself: a Witch Hunter who never learned it must cast Desecrate without ever producing a Shadowstorm.",
